{"authored" [{"question" "q-135316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the following matrix: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041215/state.json" "file_sha256" "df224c91b8d0b38c1947b469e105176f9dc50e4ac9cec766bb3e56d90c5b385b" "basis" 1491 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041215/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-135316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041215/state.json" "file_sha256" "df224c91b8d0b38c1947b469e105176f9dc50e4ac9cec766bb3e56d90c5b385b" "basis" 1491 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041215/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-135316" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041215/activity-metadata.json" "file