} {"question" "q-135397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070476/state.json" "file_sha256" "1f89989010f3075039ad99f70dfeac8431dc4a61ed72a1d546c33d74f92548f7" "basis" 2499 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070476/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-135351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the following matrix: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076405/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1a1dd1b0132b9c115a96d36c24954baae9c51747e4553c54eecda28e18ed58f"} {"question" "q-135351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & 0 & ⋯ & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076405/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1a1dd1b0132b9c115a96d36c24954baae9c51747e4553c54eecda28e18ed58f"} {"question" "q-135351" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076405/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "226520e3a6aab2ec22ff76bb50f784de30617941e763413efbf077ecccc14569"} {"question" "q-135351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076405/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1a1dd1b0132b9c115a96d36c24954baae9c51747e4553c54eecda28e18ed58f"} {"question" "q-135351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076405/state.json" "file_sha256" "d1a1dd1b0132b9c115a96d36c24954baae9c51747e4553c54eecda28e18ed58f"} {"question" "q-135351" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\sqrt{3} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end